  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Where to Begin**: back after 33 archived shows (420 days) [6]\n- **Wonderful (The Way I Feel) with Trampled by Turtles**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2012-08-10.km184.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 133 min; rated 4.75/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer judges this the better of two known recordings; the other, a Schoeps split omni source, sounds somewhat muddy by comparison; Reviewer calls it a fine recording; Reviewer finds the recording nice and clear, and worth keeping [2][3][4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Perseid meteors streaked overhead on a perfect night in Somerset, Wisconsin [2]\n- Reviewer describes an extremely spacey night, likened to a county fair, attributing the description to Jim [3]\n- Preferred over the other circulating recording of this show, which uses Schoeps microphones in a split omni setup [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2012-08-10.km184.flac16**: taped by Rick Odeen; transferred by Rick Odeen; source: Neumann skm-184 > Lunatec V3 > Busman Mod HD-P2, 24/48 [1]. Also: Chain: Neumann SKM 184 microphones, Lunatec V3, then Busman modified HD-P2, recorded at 24-bit/48 kHz; Converted to 16-bit/44.1 kHz in Samplitude with dither and resampling; recorded and transferred by Rick Odeen [1]",
